      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
          "content": "An analytical and clinical evaluation of cTnI on the ImmuliteTurbo system with 15 min assay time compared to 45 min with the original Immulite assay is presented."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS AND DESIGN",
          "content": "Detection limit, functional sensitivity, AMI decision limit, assay linearity, influence of sample material (serum, heparin, citrate and EDTA plasma), interference, analytical and clinical method comparison studies were performed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Functional sensitivity (at CV 20%) was 0.35 compared to 0.23 microg/L for the original assay. AMI decision limit (99th percentile of a reference control group) was 0.48 microg/L for both assays. In patients with acute coronary syndromes, chronic renal failure or pulmonary embolism the assays showed concordant results in 87.2-96.5%. Differing results were only found around the cut-off level and were attributed to assay imprecision."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The new assay is sensitive for the determination of cTnI, shows comparable results to the original assay version and is easy to perform within 15 min."
        }
      ]},
